its/yan\",\"id\":\"485\"},{\"name\":\"Adfox monetization\",\"href\":\"en/stat/metrics/visits/adfox\",\"id\":\"486\"},{\"name\":\"Content analytics\",\"href\":\"en/st","error":null,"capabilityHits":["routing","bank-accounts","tracking","population-stats","analytics-tracking","ads-campaigns","cloud-hosting","object-storage"]},"yandex-metrica-logs":{"url":"https://yandex.com/dev/metrika/en/logs/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-30T05:31:44.719Z","text":"Introduction | Yandex Metrica API Interface reference FAQ Introduction API architecture Authorization Quick start Additional scenarios API error descriptions Changelog Management API Data import API Reporting API Logs API Introduction Events Sessions Parametrization Connecting Logs API to ClickHouse Use scenarios Logs API reference FAQ Feedback Introduction In this article : Limitations How to increase the quota FAQ Why do the numbers I see in the Logs API and the Yandex Metrica web interface not match? Logs API Introduction Introduction Limitations How to increase the quota FAQ Why do the numbers I see in the Logs API and the Yandex Metrica web interface not match? The Logs API can be used to retrieve non-aggregated data collected by Yandex Metrica. This API is designed for users looking to process statistical data on their own to tackle their specific analytical challenges. You can store and manage the retrieved data using ClickHouse . Session data is updated as new information becomes available. On average, 99% of sessions conclude within 3 days of their start. To use the API, get an authorization token . It must be included in every API request. Requests count toward your quota . If the quota is exceeded, further user actions will be temporarily blocked. For one Yandex Metrica tag, the total size of data transmitted in requests (including logs that weren't deleted from storage) is 10 GB. Statistical information for the current day is not available, because it may be incomplete. We recommend requesting data for the previous day and earlier periods. Limitations You can request data for a period of no more than 1 year per request. The fields field, which specifies the list of fields to be exported, must not exceed 3000 characters. The total quota for downloaded data is 10 GB. This limitation applies to all prepared log files. To free up your storage quota , regularly delete both prepared and downloaded log files. This way, you can prevent exceeding the storage limit. To determine how much space is currently available to you for storing Yandex Metrica log files, get a list of your log requests and manually sum the values from the size field. How to increase the quota To increase your quota, activate Yandex Metrica Pro . FAQ Why do the numbers I see in the Logs API and the Yandex Metrica web interface not match? This might happen because the interface employs extra data processing algorithms. To ensure that this data is processed correctly, the system stores numbers using the IEEE 754 standard. The IEEE 754 standard may introduce inaccuracies in arithmetic operations. To increase the precision of calculations, the system multiplies numbers by a specific factor. Integers are handled without any loss of precision. However, the resulting values of floating-point numbers may differ from their initial values. When attempting to revert these modified numbers to their initial values, the resulting deviation depends on the level of precision allowed by the specified factor. Fields where bids apply Field Bid ym:s:purchaseRevenue 1 (also used in the Reporting API ). ym:s:goalsPrice 1000 ym:s:productsPrice 1,000,000 ym:s:impressionsProductPrice ym:s:purchaseTax ym:s:eventsProductPrice Was the article helpful? Yes No Previous Get data by time Next Events module = {}; __NONCE__ = \"H48MqefUxrWJKuBVoyI2Pw==\"; __ENV__ = \"production\"; __DATA__ = {\"err\":null,\"page\":\"/_doc\",\"pathname\":\"dev/metrika/en/logs/\",\"query\":{},\"props\":{\"pageProps\":{\"data\":{\"revision\":\"r20856727\",\"docLang\":\"en\",\"docLangs\":[\"ru\",\"en\"],\"docVersion\":null,\"docVersions\":null,\"viewerConfigParams\":{\"buildParams\":{\"strict\":true,\"breaks\":false,\"allowHTML\":true,\"singlePage\":true,\"apply-presets\":true,\"langs\":[\"ru\",\"en\"]},\"project-name\":\"dev-metrika\",\"is-new-external\":true,\"no-index\":false,\"langs\":[\"ru\",\"en\"],\"metrika\":19792447,\"favicon-src\":\"https://yastatic.net/s3/metrika/ui-projects/public/_/favicon.ico\"},\"viewerInterface\":{},\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe Logs API can be used to retrieve non-aggregated data collected by Yandex Metrica. This API is designed for users looking to process statistical data on their own to tackle their specific analytical challenges.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eYou can store and manage the retrieved data using \\u003ca href=\\\"en/logs/clickhouse-integration\\\"\\u003eClickHouse\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cdiv class=\\\"yfm-note yfm-accent-info\\\" note-type=\\\"info\\\"\\u003e\\u003cdiv class=\\\"yfm-note-content\\\"\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eSession data is updated as new information becomes available. On average, 99% of sessions conclude within 3 days of their start.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eTo use the API, \\u003ca href=\\\"en/intro/authorization\\\"\\u003eget an authorization token\\u003c/a\\u003e. It must be included in every API request. Requests count toward your \\u003ca href=\\\"en/intro/quotas\\\"\\u003equota\\u003c/a\\u003e. If the quota is exceeded, further user actions will be temporarily blocked.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eFor one Yandex Metrica tag, the total size of data transmitted in requests (including logs that weren't deleted from storage) is 10 GB.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cdiv class=\\\"yfm-note yfm-accent-info\\\" note-type=\\\"info\\\"\\u003e\\u003cdiv class=\\\"yfm-note-content\\\"\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eStatistical information for the current day is not available, because it may be incomplete. We recommend requesting data for the previous day and earlier periods.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003ch2 id=\\\"restrictions\\\"\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"en/logs/#restrictions\\\" class=\\\"yfm-anchor yfm-clipboard-anchor\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003eLimitations\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eYou can request data for a period of no more than 1 year per request.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eThe \\u003ccode class=\\\"yfm-clipboard-inline-code\\\" role=\\\"button\\\" tabindex='0' id=\\\"inline-code-id-44pr98ek\\\"\\u003efields\\u003c/code\\u003e field, which specifies the list of fields to be exported, must not exceed 3000 characters.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eThe total quota for downloaded data is 10 GB. This limitation applies to all prepared log files.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eTo free up your \\u003ca href=\\\"en/logs/openapi/clean\\\"\\u003estorage quota\\u003c/a\\u003e, regularly delete both prepared and downloaded log files. This way, you can prevent exceeding the storage limit.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cdiv class=\\\"yfm-note yfm-accent-info\\\" note-type=\\\"info\\\"\\u003e\\u003cdiv class=\\\"yfm-note-content\\\"\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eTo determine how much space is currently available to you for storing Yandex Metrica log files, get a \\u003ca href=\\\"en/logs/openapi/getLogRequests\\\"\\u003elist of your log requests\\u003c/a\\u003e and manually sum the values from the \\u003ccode class=\\\"yfm-clipboard-inline-code\\\" role=\\\"button\\\" tabindex='0' id=\\\"inline-code-id-gldk7syb\\\"\\u003esize\\u003c/code\\u003e field.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003ch3 id=\\\"quotas\\\"\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"en/logs/#quotas\\\" class=\\\"yfm-anchor yfm-clipboard-anchor\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003eHow to increase the quota\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eTo increase your quota, activate \\u003ca href=\\\"https://yandex.ru/support/metrica/pro/intro.html?lang=en\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noreferrer noopener\\\"\\u003eYandex Metrica Pro\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003ch2 id=\\\"faq\\\"\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"en/logs/#faq\\\" class=\\\"yfm-anchor yfm-clipboard-anchor\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003eFAQ\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\u003ch3 id=\\\"qanda\\\"\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"en/logs/#qanda\\\" class=\\\"yfm-anchor yfm-clipboard-anchor\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003eWhy do the numbers I see in the Logs API and the Yandex Metrica web interface not match?\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- source: en/_includes/qanda.md --\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eThis might happen because the interface employs extra data processing algorithms. To ensure that this data is processed correctly, the system stores numbers using the \\u003ca href=\\\"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/IEEE_754-2008\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noreferrer noopener\\\"\\u003eIEEE 754\\u003c/a\\u003e standard.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cdiv class=\\\"yfm-note yfm-accent-warning\\\" note-type=\\\"warning\\\"\\u003e\\u003cdiv class=\\\"yfm-note-content\\\"\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThe IEEE 754 standard may introduce inaccuracies in arithmetic operations. To increase the precision of calculations, the system multiplies numbers by a specific factor.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eIntegers are handled without any loss of precision. However, the resulting values of floating-point numbers may differ from their initial values. When attempting to revert these modified numbers to their initial values, the resulting deviation depends on the level of precision allowed by the specified factor.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\u003ch4 id=\\\"fields-with-bids\\\"\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"en/logs/#fields-with-bids\\\" class=\\\"yfm-anchor yfm-clipboard-anchor\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003eFields where bids apply\\u003c/h4\\u003e\\n\\u003ctable\\u003e\\n\\u003ctbody\\u003e\\n\\u003ctr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eField\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eBid\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003c/tr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eym:s:purchaseRevenue\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e1 (also used in the \\u003ca href=\\\"en/stat/\\\"\\u003eReporting API\\u003c/a\\u003e).\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003c/tr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eym:s:goalsPrice\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e1000\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003c/tr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eym:s:productsPrice\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd rowspan=\\\"4\\\"\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e1,000,000\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003c/tr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eym:s:impressionsProductPrice\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003c/tr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eym:s:purchaseTax\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003c/tr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctr\\u003e\\n\\u003ctd\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eym:s:eventsProductPrice\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/td\\u003e\\n\\u003c/tr\\u003e\\n\\u003c/tbody\\u003e\\n\\u003c/table\\u003e\\n\",\"title\":\"Introduction\",\"headings\":[{\"title\":\"Limitations\",\"href\":\"en/logs/#restrictions\",\"level\":2,\"items\":[{\"title\":\"How to increase the quota\",\"href\":\"en/logs/#quotas\",\"level\":3}]},{\"title\":\"FAQ\",\"href\":\"en/logs/#faq\",\"level\":2,\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Why do the numbers I see in the Logs API and the Yandex Metrica web interface not match?\",\"href\":\"en/logs/#qanda\",\"level\":3,\"items\":[]}]}],\"meta\":{\"metadata\":[{\"name\":\"generator\",\"content\":\"Diplodoc Platform v5.55.3\"}],\"alternate\":[\"en/logs/\",\"ru/logs/\",{\"h