problems, please use the feedback form 9314741556204160719 : 1788067907","error":null,"capabilityHits":[]},"yandex-pay-api":{"url":"https://pay.yandex.ru/docs/en/custom/backend/yandex-pay-api/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-30T05:31:49.185Z","text":"Overview - Yandex Pay API | Yandex Pay About Yandex Pay Merchant console Connect via API How it works Integrating by adding a Yandex Pay button Integrating by generating a form link Connecting Yandex Split Accepting payments in two steps Send receipts to the Federal Tax Service Frontend documentation Backend documentation Overview Merchant API Yandex Pay API Overview order operation subscriptions Delivery Connect via CMS Connect a payment gateway Prohibited goods Branding rules Terms and definitions Support In this article : Sections Specification Connect via API Backend documentation Yandex Pay API Overview Sections Specification Yandex Pay API version: 1.0.0 Transmit the following HTTP headers in your requests: X-Request-Id: X-Request-Timeout: X-Request-Attempt: &lt;Attempt number (0 — the first attempt, 1, 2 etc. are repeat attempts)&gt; X-Request-Id is needed to debug requests and to ensure idempotency of write requests. That's why the same value of X-Request-Id must be maintained in all the repeat requests when receiving errors with HTTP codes 5xx or 429 in response. X-Request-Timeout is needed for deadline propagation while processing a request in the system. Avoid timeout values that are less than one second. Recommended timeout values are 10-20 seconds. X-Request-Attempt is useful for general diagnostics. Authenticating the merchant's request To use the API, you need to obtain an authentication API key. Pass the token in each request in the HTTP Authorization header. The keys can be managed from the [Yandex Pay](https://console.pay.yandex.ru/settings console). In the sandbox environment, the API key is equal to the merchant_id value. --header &#x27;Authorization: Api-Key &lt;key value&gt;&#x27; If the token passed in the 