 Overview Quick start Feedback Overview In this article : Lookup Update Overview Lookup Update You can use the Safe Browsing API to check URLs for threats. The Safe Browsing list is created and maintained by Yandex. The list contains unsafe websites known for using social engineering (phishing and fraud) or hosting malicious or unwanted code. To check that a resource is safe, use one of the following interfaces: Lookup . An easy-to-use interface. This interface requires that each URL is checked on the server. It doesn't support data encryption. Update . A complex-to-implement interface. This interface enables high request frequency and low response times. The data you exchange with the server is encrypted. Lookup Using this interface, you can check a URL by sending a request to the Yandex Safe Browsing server. Advantages Simple URL check. Send a request containing a list of URLs: the server will respond whether each of them is safe. Disadvantages No privacy. The URL is sent in an unencrypted format. The server knows which URLs the user wants to check. The response time is undefined. Each request is processed by the server. Response time is not guaranteed. If you don't have any data privacy or response time requirements, use the Lookup interface. Update Using the Update interface, you can download an encrypted copy of the Safe Browsing lists and see if URLs are present on them. This interface enables high request frequency and low response times. It's used by browsers and platforms to protect many users. Advantages Privacy. The request is only sent to the server if the URL is found in the local Safe Browsing database. The URL is encrypted, and the server is agnostic of the URLs checked. Response time. The local database is a copy of the Safe Browsing lists, so you don't need to access the server every time you check a URL. Disadvantages Implementation. You need to download and periodically update a copy of the Safe Browsing lists (containing variable-length SHA256 hashes). Sophisticated URL check. You need to canonicalize the URL, create multiple expressions for the host and path, and compute the SHA256 hash (to check the local copy against the server-hosted list). If you care about data privacy and response times, use the Update interface. Was the article helpful? Yes No Next Quick start","error":null,"capabilityHits":["url-safety"]},"yandex-turbo-pages":{"url":"https://yandex.com/dev/turbo/doc/en/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-30T05:31:57.895Z","text":"About Turbo pages | Turbo pages About Turbo pages Warning Since April 2, Turbo pages are no longer displayed in the search. For more information, see the webmaster's blog . Read more about the benefits of Turbo pages in our PDF ## Generating Turbo pages {#formation} Turbo pages can be generated via an RSS feed. For more information, see [Turning on Turbo pages for content sites](quick-start/articles.md). {% note info %} For some media sites, Turbo pages are already generated with Autoparsing. For more information, see [Connecting Turbo pages generated with autoparsing](quick-start/autoparsing.md). {% endnote %} ## Displaying Turbo pages in Yandex {#display-test} #### What it looks like ![](_assets/page-example.png) #### Examples of search snippets There are several types of snippets that can be shown in search results. The type depends on the site content. Examples: {% cut \"Standard snippet\" %} ![](_assets/turbo-snippet-standart.png) {% endcut %} {% cut \"Fact answer\" %} ![](_assets/turbo-snippet-povar-rate.png) {% endcut %} {% cut \"Recipe carousel\" %} ![](_assets/turbo-snippet-povar-carusel.png) {% endcut %} {% cut \"News summary\" %} ![](_assets/turbo-snippet-search-news-list.png) {% endcut %} {% cut \"News carousel\" %} ![](_assets/turbo-snippet-search-news-carusel.png) {% endcut %} {% cut \"Recent news\" %} ![](_assets/turbo-snippet-search-news-time.png) {% endcut %} #### **How to enable** : See instructions for turning on Turbo pages [for media sites](quick-start/articles.md)